    "lawCode": "Amd §130, Pub Serv L",
    "lawSection": "Public Service Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S3713\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to amend the public service law, in relation to powers of\nmunicipalities and state agencies\n\n\n PURPOSE OF THE BILL :\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to clarify the authority of municipalities\nand state agencies to require, upon express authority of the Public\nService Commission (Commission), conditions for construction or\noperation of major electric or gas transmission facilities.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1 of this bill would amend Public Service Law (PSL) § 130 to\nclarify that, upon express authority of the Commission, state agencies\nand municipalities may require any approval, consent, permit, or other\ncondition for the construction or operation of a major electric or gas\ntransmission facility. It would also provide that state agencies and\nmunicipalities may require, without the Commission's express\nauthority, conditions established in otherwise applicable state or\nlocal laws for the administration and enforcement of the New York\nState Uniform Fire Prevention and Building Code (Building Code).\n\nSection 2 of this bill provides that this bill would take effect\nimmediately and apply to all petitions filed on or after the effective\ndate.\n\n EXISTING LAW\n\nPrior to preparation of a site for construction of a major electric or\ngas transmission facility in the State (PSL Article VII), a person is\nrequired to obtain from the Commission a Certificate of Environmental\nCompatibility and Public Need. When the Commission issues its\ndetermination, it is required to, among other things, find and\ndetermine that the facility conforms to applicable state and local\nlaws. The Commission may refuse to apply any local requirement that it\nfinds to be unreasonably restrictive in view of technology, cost,\neconomics or the needs of consumers located inside or outside of the\nmunicipality (PSL §126(1)(t)).\n\nPSL § 130 provides that, notwithstanding any other provision of law,\nno state agency or municipality can require any approval, consent,\npermit, certificate or other condition for the construction or\noperation of a major transmission facility that is the subject of an\nArticle VII application, other than worker protection requirements\nduring facility construction and operation.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nThis is a new proposal.\n\n STATEMENT IN SUPPORT :\n\nThe purpose of PSL Article VII is to provide a single forum, open to\ncitizens, groups.  municipalities and other public agencies, for the\nresolution of all matters, including state and local requirements,\nrelating to the siting of major electric and gas transmission\nfacilities.\n\nThe provisions or Article VII relating to stale and local laws do not\nexplicitly state that the Commission may authorize the application of\ncertain state and local requirements to the construction and operation\nof specific major electric or gas transmission facilities.  Express\nauthorization would allow state and local authorities to apply and\nenforce requirements of specific local impact that are not suitable\nfor Commission approval and enforcement. For example, to ensure public\nsafety and the unimpeded flow of traffic, the Commission may authorize\na state or local department of transportation to require a highway\nwork permit before a holder of an Article VII siting certificate\nenters and performs work such as excavation or wire-pulling on a\npublic highway right-of-way.\n\nAmong the stated purposes of the Building Code (Executive Law (EL)\nArticle 18; 9 NYCRR 600 (et seq.) is the requirement that the Building\nCode be in full force and effect in every area of the State, and to\nencourage local governments to exercise their full powers to\nadminister and enforce the Code (EL 9371 (2)(c) and (d). The Building\nCode provides reasonably uniform standards for the construction and\nconstruction materials of public and private buildings (Exec. L.\n§377(2), and thus may apply to such facilities as substations,\nswitching stations, transition stations, compressor stations and\nconverter stations.  Adoption of this proposed amendment would clarify\nthat Building Code administration and enforcement regarding major\nutility transmission facilities is best left to State and municipal\nentities already empowered to administer and enforce the Building\nCode.\n\nIn sum, this bill would clarify the ability of the Commission to\nauthorize the application of state and local laws to the construction\nand/or operation of major transmission facilities, and would provide\nfor enforcement of applicable provisions of the Building Code to such\nfacilities.\n\n BUDGET IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis bill would take effect immediately and apply to all petitions\nfiled on or after the effective date.\n",
